      "id": "62081469-2323-4257-be2a-76bff6eadfda",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "class Main {\r\n\r\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\r\n\r\n        System.out.println(\"Hello World\");\r\n\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// class Main → Defines a class named Main.\r\n\r\n// main() → The main entry point of a traditional Java application.Code execution starts from main() method.\r\n\r\n// public → Makes the method accessible to the JVM.\r\n\r\n// static → Allows the JVM to call the method without creating an object.\r\n\r\n// void → Indicates that the method does not return a value.\r\n\r\n// String[] args → Stores command-line arguments.\r\n\r\n// System.out.println() → Prints output to the console.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "62081469-2323-4257-be2a-76bff6eadfda",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 10,
          "success": true
